-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY FIRMWARE FILES — EXCEPTION TO THE ABOVE LICENSE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT grant above applies only to the original work of this repository's
author: the research notes, the reverse-engineering write-ups, and the tools
written for this project (`work/asusauth.py`, `work/emu.py`, `work/disasm.py`,
`work/unlock.py`, `unlock_mitm_addon.py`, `mega_dl.py`, and documentation).

This repository also contains, for research, verification and interoperability
purposes only, a small number of files extracted from original ASUS firmware
("Third-Party Firmware Files"):

  - work/abl_linuxloader.efi   — the ABL bootloader image (PE32+ ARM64)
                                 extracted from the ASUS
                                 "31.1010.0410.61" (Android 12) RAW firmware
                                 package for the ZenFone 8 (I006D).
  - work/asus_bl_cert.der      — the ASUS unlock certificate embedded in ABL.
  - scripts/*.sh                — the ASUS flash scripts shipped inside the
                                 same RAW firmware package.

NO LICENSE IS GRANTED IN THESE THIRD-PARTY FIRMWARE FILES. All rights in them
belong to ASUSTeK Computer Inc. (and, where applicable, their other original
rightsholders). They are reproduced here solely to make the published research
independently verifiable, and to allow the unlock tool to be tested against
the exact bootloader image it was engineered from.

THIS REPOSITORY DOES NOT REDISTRIBUTE FIRMWARE PACKAGES. The complete RAW
firmware images, OTA update packages, and ASUS applications (APKs) that this
research was performed against are NOT included here. Obtain any firmware
you need directly from ASUS or from the community archives linked in the
README, and comply with the terms under which it is made available.

If you are a rightsholder and object to the presence of any Third-Party
Firmware File in this repository, open an issue or contact the author and it
will be removed promptly.
